Bundled third-party libraries
================================================================================

The distributed application bundle embeds the following libraries in
`Contents/Frameworks/`. They are redistributed unmodified, and their own license
terms apply to them rather than the GPL terms above.

HDF5
    https://www.hdfgroup.org/
    Copyright (C) The HDF Group and the Board of Trustees of the University of
    Illinois. Distributed under the HDF5 BSD-style license.
    License text: `Licenses/HDF5-LICENSE.txt`.

libaec (Adaptive Entropy Coding library)
    https://gitlab.dkrz.de/k202009/libaec
    Copyright (C) Deutsches Klimarechenzentrum GmbH. BSD 2-Clause license.
    License text: `Licenses/libaec-LICENSE.txt`.

libsz (szip compatibility interface, provided by libaec)
    Covered by the libaec license above.

The full license text for each ships in the application bundle at
`Contents/Resources/Licenses/`, from the `Licenses/` directory in this
repository. Verified in a built bundle on 2026-09-09, not assumed.

Identity of the three committed binaries, so that what is redistributed is
stated rather than described. SHA-256, byte size, and the `LC_ID_DYLIB` current
version each binary declares:

    libhdf5.dylib   c374776deeb3e4b12874ca8d5e7aad1837a70d9363885cc742302f9d98283c64
                    4 285 968 B, current version 320.1.1; the binary's own
                    version string reads "HDF5 library version: 2.1.1"
    libaec.0.dylib  166a8041fb067358993cd456f1d189631e2fd7931371e46a22d191bcc461b8a5
                    52 848 B, current version 2.7.0; the binary retains the
                    build path `libaec-v1.1.7`
    libsz.2.dylib   6ebc2e1c15e432564acdb33875ab14d977c63589402929f5c274de1b46d4774b
                    53 280 B, current version 3.1.0; built with libaec above

They were built by Homebrew on the maintainer's machine and committed on
2026-08-25; `libhdf5.dylib` still carries its build stamp
`Installation point: /opt/homebrew/Cellar/hdf5/2.1.1` and HDF5's compiled-in
default plugin search path under the same prefix, which is how the version is
established from the binary rather than from a note. No load command in any of
the three names an absolute path. The license texts here were taken
from those two Homebrew installations. There is no automated rebuild path: the
binaries are what the hashes above name, and nothing in the repository can
reproduce them from source (`docs/open-items.md`).


================================================================================
Machine-learned models
================================================================================

No third-party model weights are distributed with mac4DSTEM. The stock
Ultralytics `yolov8n.mlpackage` (AGPL-3.0) that was added to the Xcode project
on 2026-09-05 as a reference was never part of a shipped build and was removed
from the tree on 2026-09-07. abTEM (GPL-3.0) is used only as a simulation tool
during development; nothing from it is distributed. Any detector mac4DSTEM
ships is trained on its own data with its own weights.
